{ He has just offered the pawn on b5. Do you remember how to punish it? }
9... b5 { Take it. But with which piece? Think before you grab. } 10. Nxb5 { Yes, the knight. } (10. Bxb5 { Not this one. Now his knight jump to e4 really works. } 10... Nxe4 11. Nxe4 Qa5+ 12. Nfd2 Qxb5 { He has it all back and the game is level. }) (10. O-O { You had to take that pawn. Now he simply rolls forward. } 10... b4 11. Na4 Ba6 12. Re1 Bxd3 13. Qxd3 Qd7 { He owns the queen side. }) 10... Nxe4 { He throws another piece at you. It does not work. } 11. Bxe4 { The only capture, and you are a piece up. } (11. O-O { You left a free knight on the board. } 11... Re8 12. Re1 a6 13. Nc3 Nxc3 14. bxc3 { Level again. }) 11... Re8 { The pin. What can defend the bishop on e4? } 12. Ng5 { Well spotted. } (12. O-O { The pin is gone, and so is the bishop. } 12... Rxe4 13. Nc3 Re8 14. Bg5 Qd7 { Given back. }) (12. Nd2 { It defends, but it is passive and slow. } 12... Ba6 13. a4 Qa5 14. Nxd6 Nd7 { Messy. }) (12. Qe2 { Now your queen is pinned too. } 12... Ba6 13. a4 Qa5+ 14. Kd1 Bxb5 { Your king is stuck in the middle. }) 12... Qa5+ { Check, and the knight on b5 hangs. There is one move only. } 13. Nc3 { That is it. Block and hold everything together. } (13. Kf1 { The knight on b5 drops. } 13... Qxb5+ 14. Kg1 Nd7 15. Bc2 Qb4 { Gone. }) (13. Bd2 { This drops it too. } 13... Qxb5 14. Qf3 f5 15. Bc3 Bxc3+ { It falls apart. }) (13. Qd2 { And so does this. } 13... Qxb5 14. a4 Qc4 15. Kd1 Nd7 { You are worse. }) 13... h6 { He kicks the knight. Remember what you did here. } 14. Ne6 { Nice, that is the one. The knight cannot be touched. } (14. O-O { Safe, but the knight on g5 is simply lost now. } 14... hxg5 15. Re1 Qd8 16. Bf3 Rxe1+ { A whole piece given away. }) (14. Bd2 { This hands him the knight as well. } 14... hxg5 15. O-O Qd8 16. Bc2 g4 { Gone. }) 1-0


[Event "Benoni for white: he declines with rook e8"]
[Result "1-0"]
