[SetUp "1"]
[Site "https://lichess.org/analysis/rnbq1rk1/p4pbp/3p1np1/1NpP4/4P3/3B1N1P/PP3PP1/R1BQK2R_b_KQ_-_0_10"]

{ He does not take on e4. He puts the rook there instead. You are a pawn up. }
10... Re8 { The main try. He leans on your pawn at e4 instead of grabbing it. } 11. O-O { Calm and correct. The king is safe and the extra pawn stays yours. } (11. Nd2 { This defends the pawn, but the knight gets clumsy. } 11... Nxd5 12. Nc4 Re6 13. O-O Nb4 { He is level again. }) (11. Nc3 { Now the pawn on e4 falls with a free move. } 11... Nxe4 12. Nxe4 f5 13. Bg5 Qd7 { All equal. }) (11. Bg5 { This leaves the pawn hanging with a check to follow. } 11... c4 12. Bxc4 Rxe4+ 13. Be2 Qa5+ { Your king is caught in the middle. }) (11. Qe2 { The queen blocks her own bishop and the pawn still falls. } 11... Nxe4 12. Bxe4 Ba6 13. a4 Qa5+ { Very uncomfortable. }) 11... Nxe4 { Now he takes. How do you take back? } 12. Bxe4 { The bishop. He must take back with the rook, and your extra pawn survives. } (12. Re1 { You keep the bishop, but the knight escapes and your pawn goes. } 12... a6 13. Nc3 Nf6 14. Rxe8+ Nxe8 { Nothing left. }) (12. Bf4 { The knight is still sitting there, and now he kicks yours. } 12... a6 13. Na3 Nf6 14. Qb3 Bf8 { Only equal. }) (12. Qa4 { The bishop still hangs to that knight. } 12... Bd7 13. Bf4 a6 14. Qa3 Bxb5 { Level. }) (12. Qb3 { The queen hits d5 and f7, but the knight on e4 is still alive. } 12... Qb6 13. Bf4 Nd7 14. Rad1 Rb8 { All level, and the extra pawn is gone. }) 12... Rxe4 { Forced. Now his rook sits in the middle of the board. } 13. Nc3 { The knight comes home with a free hit on the rook. A clean extra pawn. [%cal Gc3e4] } (13. Bg5 { Just as good, and also pleasant for you. } 13... Qd7 14. Nc3 Re8 15. Qd2 Na6 { The same thing, one move later. }) (13. Re1 { Trading rooks helps him, not you. } 13... Rxe1+ 14. Qxe1 Nd7 15. Bf4 Bb7 { Much less pressure. }) (13. a4 { Too slow. His bishop grabs the pawn on b2. } 13... Ba6 14. Bd2 Bxb2 15. Bg5 Qf8 { All level again. }) 1-0


