{ The pawn is yours. Now he pokes the knight with the a pawn. Where does it go? }
10... a6 { The knight is attacked. Two squares look possible, and only one is right. } 11. Nc3 { Home, towards the middle. From c3 it guards e4 and eyes b5 again. [%csl Ge4] } (11. Na3 { The rim is the wrong way. Out there the knight does nothing. } 11... Re8 12. O-O Nxe4 13. Re1 Nf6 14. Rxe8+ Nxe8 { Your extra pawn is gone and the knight is homeless. }) (11. Nxd6 { Greedy. The queen takes and your centre collapses. } 11... Qxd6 12. e5 Qe7 13. d6 Qe8 14. O-O Nfd7 { A whole piece for two pawns. }) (11. Qa4 { The knight is still hanging, and now the pawn comes at you. } 11... c4 12. Nxd6 cxd3 13. Bf4 Qd7 { You are losing this. }) 11... Nbd7 { He develops. Now put a bishop where it hurts. } 12. Bf4 { Straight at the pawn on d6, his weakest point. [%csl Rd6][%cal Gf4d6] } (12. O-O { Just as good. Safety first is never a bad rule. } 12... Nh5 13. Be3 Rb8 14. Rb1 Re8 { A fine game, and a pawn up. }) (12. Be3 { Also good, and it eyes the pawn on c5. } 12... h6 13. Qd2 g5 14. h4 g4 { Sharp, but still yours. }) (12. Rb1 { Slow. He gets his knight going first. } 12... Nh5 13. Bg5 f6 14. Be3 Qe7 { Some of the grip has gone. }) 12... Qe7 { He defends the pawn. Now finish the job. } 13. O-O { King safe, pawn up, every piece working. That is a dream Benoni. } (13. Qd2 { Also strong. But castling first is simply cleaner. } 13... Nh5 14. Bh6 Ne5 15. Nxe5 Bxh6 { Still very good for you. }) (13. Be3 { Now the knight jump frees him. } 13... Nxe4 14. Nxe4 c4 15. Bc2 f5 { He is back in the game. }) 1-0


