{[%eval +1.12] You are a whole piece up and he checks straight away. Do not lose your head.} 1... Qa5+ {[%eval +2.01] Check, and the knight on b5 is attacked as well. Find the move that saves both.} 2. Nc3 {[%eval +2.12] [%cal Gc3c3]The only one. The knight blocks the check and defends itself.}  (2. Nd2 {This blocks, but the knight on b5 just falls.}  Qxb5 3. a4 Qa6 4. Bf3 Re8+ {The piece went back for nothing.})  (2. Kf1 {Running costs the knight and your castling.}  Qxb5+ 3. Bd3 Qb7 4. Kg1 Qxd5 {He is on top now.})  (2. Qd2 {The queen block also drops the knight.}  Qxb5 3. a4 Qe8 4. Qe3 Ba6 {You are worse.})  (2. Bd2 {And so does this one.}  Qxb5 3. Qc2 Ba6 4. Bc3 Bxc3+ {It all falls apart.}) f5 {[%eval +2.40] He hits your bishop. Where does it belong?} 3. Bc2 {[%eval +2.03] [%cal Gc2h7]Back to c2, still looking down the diagonal at his king.}  (3. O-O {Also winning. But you hand the bishop back for a pawn.}  fxe4 4. Nxe4 Qb6 5. Re1 Nd7 {Still much better, just a lot less.})  (3. Bxf5 {Do not trade your extra piece off.}  Bxf5 4. O-O Nd7 5. Re1 Nb6 {Most of your edge has gone.})  (3. Bd3 {The pawn comes on and the bishop is loose.}  Bxc3+ 4. bxc3 Qxc3+ 5. Qd2 Re8+ {Suddenly you are the one in trouble.}) Bxc3+ {[%eval +2.43] He takes the blocker. Recapture with the pawn.} 4. bxc3 {[%eval +2.41] Right. The king still has squares.}  (4. Kf1 {Now his bishop eats on b2 and the rook follows.}  Bxb2 5. Bxb2 Qb5+ 6. Kg1 Qxb2 {Everything is level.})  (4. Bd2 {This gives the whole piece back.}  Re8+ 5. Kf1 Bxd2 6. Nxd2 Ba6+ {You are worse.}) Ba6 {[%eval +2.28] His bishop stops you castling. Your king must walk.} 5. Kd2 {[%eval +2.29] [%cal Gd2c1]Brave and correct. The king steps up and heads for the queen side.}  (5. Bb2 {Too slow. The check on e8 wins your bishop.}  Re8+ 6. Kd2 Be2 7. Qb1 Nd7 {Your edge is nearly gone.})  (5. Ba4 {The bishop wanders off and he grabs on c3.}  Qxc3+ 6. Bd2 Qc4 7. Ng5 h6 {Only a small edge left.})  (5. Qd2 {The check comes anyway, and now with force.}  Re8+ 6. Kd1 Be2+ 7. Ke1 Bxf3+ {You are losing.}) 1-0

