{[%eval +1.17] He pokes your knight on g5 before he checks. Where does it belong?} 1... h6 {[%eval +1.37] The knight is attacked. Going back gives the whole piece away.} 2. Ne6 {[%eval +1.54] [%cal Rg8g8]Forward. If he takes with the f pawn you castle, and the bishop crashes into g6.}  (2. O-O {Safe, but the knight on g5 is simply lost.}  hxg5 3. Bd3 a6 4. Nc3 g4 {A piece for nothing.})  (2. Nxf7 {Tempting, but there is nothing there.}  Rxe4+ 3. Kf1 Kxf7 4. Qf3+ Bf5 {You are worse.})  (2. Qc2 {The knight is still hanging on g5.}  hxg5 3. O-O a6 4. Na3 a5 {Given away.})  (2. Qa4 {Same problem. The knight drops.}  hxg5 3. O-O Bd7 4. Bd3 a6 {You are worse.}) Qa5+ {[%eval +1.51] The check arrives anyway. One move keeps it all together.} 3. Nc3 {[%eval +1.61] Blocked and held. You are back in the main line, a piece up.}  (3. Kf1 {Running drops the knight on b5.}  Qxb5+ 4. Bd3 Qxd3+ 5. Qxd3 Ba6 {The extra piece is gone.})  (3. Bd2 {The bishop block loses the knight too.}  Qxb5 4. f3 fxe6 5. Kf2 Bb7 {You are lost.})  (3. Ke2 {The king walk is far too early.}  Qxb5+ 4. Kf3 fxe6 5. Kg3 Bb7 {Your king is in a net.}) 1-0

