{ His knight hops to h5 straight away, dreaming of f4. Do not panic about it. }
9... Nh5 { The knight is out early, eyeing f4. What is the calmest reply? } 10. O-O { Just castle. His knight on the edge is going nowhere useful. } (10. Be2 { Also good, and it already looks at the knight. But castle first. } 10... Nf6 11. O-O Nbd7 12. Qc2 Rb8 { The same kind of game. }) (10. Bg5 { Playable. The bishop pokes at him, and he pokes back. } 10... Bf6 11. Bh6 Bg7 12. Qd2 Nd7 { Even trade offers. }) (10. a4 { A good move in general, but the king comes first here. } 10... Nd7 11. Be2 Re8 12. O-O Nhf6 { Fine, just a different order. }) (10. g4 { Never open the door in front of your own king. } 10... Nf6 11. Bg5 h6 12. Bh4 Nbd7 { Your king side is full of holes. }) 10... Nd7 { He brings the other knight out. Ask the one on h5 what it is doing there. } 11. Be2 { The bishop steps back and stares straight at the lonely knight. [%cal Ge2h5] } (11. a4 { Good, but the knight on h5 was the thing to hit. } 11... Ne5 12. Be2 Nxf3+ 13. Bxf3 Nf6 { He got his trade. }) (11. Bg5 { The bishop is chased and the knight is left alone. } 11... Bf6 12. Be3 Re8 13. g4 Ng7 { Messy for both. }) (11. Re1 { Solid, but nothing is asked of the knight. } 11... a6 12. Bg5 Bf6 13. Bh6 Re8 { He is comfortable. }) (11. Be3 { It guards c5, but h5 is the loose piece. } 11... Re8 12. Qc2 a6 13. a4 Ne5 { He untangled easily. }) 11... Nhf6 { The knight has to come home. You gained a free move. } 12. Bf4 { And now the bishop takes aim at d6, exactly where you want it. [%csl Rd6] } (12. Bg5 { Also good. Either bishop square annoys him. } 12... h6 13. Bf4 Qe7 14. Re1 Nh7 { The same idea. }) (12. Qc2 { Fine, but the bishop move is more to the point. } 12... Rb8 13. a4 a6 14. Bg5 h6 { A little slower. }) (12. Be3 { It guards c5. But d6 is the sore spot. } 12... Qe7 13. Qc2 a6 14. a4 Rb8 { Playable. }) (12. a4 { Good idea, but the bishop wanted a square first. } 12... Re8 13. Qc2 Qe7 14. Re1 Nxe4 { Careful, that jump is real. }) 1-0


